<title>USA: Republic of Turkey may tap U.S. corp debt market.</title>
<headline>Republic of Turkey may tap U.S. corp debt market.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Republic of Turkey is expected to tap the U.S. corporate debt market with between $250 million and $500 million in debt, syndicate sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The offering is expected to consist of a five-year maturity and is rumored to come to market in April, sources  said.</p>
<p>JP Morgan Securities and SBC Warburg are expected to underwrite the deal, they added.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>(( --Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
</text>
